Only review it after doing so for the last 3 Inheritance packages.


Create a parent.java & a child.java class files.
        - Both should be utility files (Non contain the main statement/ @Test annotation 
                                        where the controller starts executing)
                                        
        - One will find out that:
         	 no object creating is necessary of the child class in the child class in order
         	 to access the method(s) present in the parent class.
         	 
